### Multicast DNS Conflict Resolution using TSR
- **Presenter:** Esko Dijk
- **Slide Deck:** [Multicast DNS conflict resolution using the Time Since Received (TSR) EDNS option](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-dnssd-multicast-dns-conflict-resolution-using-the-time-since-received-tsr-edns-option-00)
- **Draft:** `draft-ietf-dnssd-tsr`

#### Technical Presentation & Updates
- Resolves apparent mDNS conflicts when multiple proxy/router instances (e.g., SNAC routers) advertise identical service records.
- Updates in version 04:
  - Formalized TSR time comparison using a 2-second tolerance window.
  - Added guidance to maintain high internal time resolution and use explicit rounding when converting to 1-second TSR EDNS fields.
  - Rewrote section on suppressing redundant probing across mDNS registrants.
  - Imported terminology from RFC 9499.
  - Mandated that mDNS goodbye announcements MUST include the TSR option.

#### Discussion & Refinements
- **SRP Hints Field:** Ted Lemon proposed incorporating a 32-bit hash of the SRP update into the TSR option. This payload hash allows receivers to conclusively identify identical data updates regardless of timing jitter.
- **Document Scope & Title:** Ted Lemon and Esko Dijk noted the draft has expanded from defining the TSR EDNS option to specifying broader multi-advertiser cooperation behavior. The title and abstract will be updated to reflect this scope.
- **Redundant Goodbye & Primary/Secondary Roles:** Discussed adding explicit primary and secondary roles for mDNS registrants to prevent redundant goodbye broadcasts and handle fallback if a primary registrant disconnects.
- **Non-Delayed Responses:** Primary/secondary designations will also resolve potential storm issues with non-delayed mDNS responses (RFC 6762).

