### DNS-SD Data Block Introduction
- **Presenter:** Smith Kennedy
- **Slide Deck:** [DNS-SD Data Block Introduction](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-dnssd-dns-sd-data-block-introduction-00)

#### Technical Content
- Proposed a compact binary payload format (DNSSD Data Block / DDB) to convey standard DNS-SD service names and TXT/SRV records over non-IP link layer transports (Bluetooth LE Transport Discovery Service, NFC Connection Handover, Wi-Fi Aware/Direct).
- Designed for environments where network infrastructure blocks multicast DNS or where pre-association service filtering is needed before bringing up an IP link.
- **Payload Constraints:**
  - BLE Legacy Advertising: ~26 octets (with TDS overhead).
  - NFC Record Descriptor: ~32 octets.
  - Extended BLE Advertising: Up to 252 octets.
- **Discussion:**
  - Stuart Cheshire strongly supported the initiative, emphasizing the high architectural value of leveraging the unified IANA Service Name Registry (RFC 6763) across non-IP technologies instead of creating fragmented per-technology service dictionaries.
  - Lorenzo Colitti inquired about address resolution prior to IP connectivity. Smith Kennedy clarified that pre-association DDB advertisements enable application-level filtering (e.g., filtering for printing services prior to triggering link establishment or pairing).

